{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>I</b>: As you believe that I, YHWH, stand forever, take pleasure in seeking with your mouth every desire and wish of your heart, and I will fill it — not in the days of the Judges or the prophecy of the First Temple, if this Asaph is the poet in the days of David."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 81, :notes {0 "The comment appears to distinguish between the promise of answered prayer in the wilderness era versus later periods; the final conditional clause attaches to the psalm's attribution."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:35:44.063856378Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}